(Modified 2026-11-05 by Daniel Ruttley: added Windows instructions, see CHANGES.md)

This software requires the following libraries:

	- Qt >= 4.4 (Qt 5 is supported)

To compile this software, type:

	qmake
	make

To install this software, type:

	make install


Windows (10/11)
---------------

1. Install MSYS2 from https://www.msys2.org (no account needed).

2. Open the "MSYS2 UCRT64" terminal and install the compiler and Qt 5:

	pacman -Syu
	pacman -S mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-gcc mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-make mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-qt5-base

3. In the same terminal, go to this directory and build:

	qmake-qt5
	mingw32-make

   (MSYS2 names the Qt 5 qmake "qmake-qt5"; plain "qmake" is Qt 6.)

   The program is built as release/GaussianBeam-NG.exe.

4. To run it outside the MSYS2 terminal (e.g. by double-clicking), copy
   the required Qt DLLs next to the executable:

	pacman -S mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-qt5-tools
	windeployqt-qt5 release/GaussianBeam-NG.exe

   Alternatively, build a single self-contained .exe (no DLLs needed) with
   the static Qt package:

	pacman -S mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-qt5-static
	mingw32-make distclean
	/ucrt64/qt5-static/bin/qmake
	mingw32-make
